tedly returns to its initial delay, and heartbeats can advertise recovery without any successful contact with Ring. This follows from the cached getLocations contract in ring-client.ts and the inventory retry path in Ingest; the existing failure tests inject errors into getLocations instead, so they do not cover this case. Separate cached access from network-attempt accounting, or otherwise require an actual successful Ring request before clearing the circuit and unavailable status. Add a regression covering repeated inventory refresh failures after warming the location cache.","finding_id":"finding-dee3e16653738158","lineage_id":"lin-ab5dbb955ab2040e","location":"bridge/src/connector/access/ring-adapter/ring-api-adapter.ts:113","relevance":"current","resolution":"open","severity":"minor","source_local_id":"R001","title":"Do not let cached Ring reads reset the outage circuit"}],"harness_id":"codex-cli-file-primary","run_id":"run-20261107-160555736-14798783","runtime_outcome":"completed","schema_version":"1.0","started_at":"2026-11-07T16:07:35.8146097+00:00","summary":"Completed risk-based inspection of the frozen target's implemented components, covering enrollment and authentication, link framing and reconnect behavior, durable delivery, Ring integration, secret handling and logging, SQL transactions and migrations, public contracts, and verification configuration. One major resilience defect was established. The controller's single declared governance verification succeeded for this digest. No tests, builds, installers, or repository automation were run by the reviewer. Planned, unimplemented iteration work and explicitly recorded pilot limitations were distinguished from defects in existing code.","target_digest":"8f2698f30dddd8390a52056f7f134a054957681e","termination_verified":true,"validation":"valid","verdict":"findings"}